{% if rtk %}
## RTK Query

A typed `createApi` endpoint set — one entry per model operation and per
procedure, `providesTags`/`invalidatesTags` derived from the schema (a
`mutation procedure` invalidates every model its own arguments/return type
reference; a model's `create`/`update`/`delete` invalidate that model's
list and/or item tags the usual RTK Query way). Dispatches through
`@cratestack/adapter-rtk`'s base query on an RPC-transport schema, or
through this package's own REST client on a REST-transport schema —
never a second transport implementation.

```tsx
import { configureStore } from "@reduxjs/toolkit";
import { createCratestackRtkApi, {{ client_class_name }} } from "{{ package_name }}";

const client = new {{ client_class_name }}("https://api.example.com");
export const api = createCratestackRtkApi(client);

export const store = configureStore({
  reducer: { [api.reducerPath]: api.reducer },
  middleware: (getDefaultMiddleware) => getDefaultMiddleware().concat(api.middleware),
});
```
{% if models %}
```tsx
function {{ models[0].name }}List() {
  const list = api.useList{{ models[0].name }}Query();
  const [create] = api.useCreate{{ models[0].name }}Mutation();

  if (list.isLoading) {
    return null;
  }
  return <ListView data={list.data} onCreate={(input) => create(input)} />;
}
```
{% endif %}

