## SWR (file-per-model layout + hooks)

This package also carries the `swr` layout under `src/swr/` — one file per model (types
plus plain, framework-free `async` functions), a sibling `.hooks.ts` per model/procedures
file with `useSWR`/`useSWRMutation` hooks wrapping those functions, and a shared
`swrKeys` cache-key factory. It coexists with the layout documented above; nothing here
changes what's exported from the package root.

```ts
import { CratestackRuntime } from "{{ package_name }}/swr";
import { useWidget } from "{{ package_name }}/swr/models/widget.hooks";
```

Import exactly the functions/hooks you call. `swr`/React are only required if you import
a `.hooks` module — plain functions (`{{ package_name }}/swr/models/<model>`) need
nothing but the runtime. See `{{ package_name }}/swr`'s own module for the full model
list, and `{{ package_name }}/swr/procedures`/`/swr/procedures.hooks` for procedures.
{% if is_rest_transport and has_versioned_model %}

This layout gets the same optimistic-concurrency round trip the root layout's
`getWithResponse` documents above, as its own plain function per model —
`get{{ models[0].name }}WithResponse` — with the same `Decimal` revival
`get{{ models[0].name }}` applies (reaching for `runtime.getWithResponse()` directly
skips that revival and hands back an unrevived value):

```ts
import { get{{ models[0].name }}WithResponse, update{{ models[0].name }} } from "{{ package_name }}/swr/models/{{ models[0].file_stem }}";

const { value: item, response } = await get{{ models[0].name }}WithResponse(runtime, id);
const etag = response.headers.get("etag");

await update{{ models[0].name }}(runtime, id, patch, { ifMatch: etag ?? undefined });
```
{% endif %}

**One `CratestackRuntime` per surface.** The root and `/swr` each construct their own
`CratestackRuntime` class from the same template, so the two are structurally identical
but *not* interchangeable at the type level (private fields make them nominally distinct
classes) — a runtime built via `new {{ client_class_name }}(...)`'s constructor or the
root's own `CratestackRuntime` will not type-check against a `/swr` function or hook, and
vice versa. Construct the runtime from whichever surface you're calling into, and keep
that choice consistent within one component/module.
{%- endif %}
